  {
    "issue": "CSV import produces garbled or misaligned columns",
    "fix": "Export format varies by accounting tool (QuickBooks vs Xero vs a raw bank export). Open the raw CSV and check its actual header row, then update COLUMN_MAP in ingest.py to match what you actually got - not what you assumed."
  },
  {
    "issue": "AI request failed: No AI provider configured",
    "fix": "Add either AI_PROVIDER=gemini plus GEMINI_API_KEY=... (free, from aistudio.google.com/apikey), or AI_PROVIDER=claude plus ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... (from console.anthropic.com/settings/keys) to your .env file, in the same folder as sdt_ai.py."
  },
  {
    "issue": "Currency symbols render as garbled characters on charts",
    "fix": "matplotlib needs a font that supports your currency symbol (e.g. ₦) - either install one, or format axis/label text without the raw currency symbol (use the currency code, like 'NGN', instead)."
  },
  {
    "issue": "Month-over-month growth or margin shows wildly wrong percentages",
    "fix": "This shouldn't happen - compute_metrics() already guards every division against a zero denominator. If you're still seeing a strange number, check that your date column actually parsed correctly (a bad date silently groups a transaction into the wrong month, which can shift which month is 'latest')."
  },
  {
    "issue": "PDF assembly fails with an image error",
    "fix": "Confirm each chart image is fully saved and closed before building the PDF - charts.py's make_revenue_chart() and make_expense_pie() already call plt.close() after every savefig(), so this usually means a chart PNG from a previous, interrupted run is corrupted on disk. Delete revenue.png/expenses.png and regenerate them."
  },
  {
    "issue": "The AI commentary doesn't mention any of your actual numbers",
    "fix": "This is exactly what commentary.py's mentions_real_numbers() guard exists to catch - if you saw the warning printed, read the commentary and consider re-running write_commentary() (models are non-deterministic; a second attempt often engages with the real figures)."
  }
]$tsh$::jsonb,
  $res$[
  {
    "url": "https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/",
    "title": "pandas Documentation"
  },
  {
